{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DominationSqueeze","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DominationSqueeze","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WithBot","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.squeeze","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.squeeze","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L249-L258","doc":"**The ordered-field squeeze, recovered.** `ordω(cost) > ordω(budget)` —\ni.e. `val cost < val budget` — gives `budget < cost`, which is exactly what\n`rem:collatz-surreal-bound`, `rem:p-vs-np-surreal-bound` and\n`rem:ns-surreal-bound` invoke. Nothing is lost by taking the algebraic core as\nprimitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.lt_of_val_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.lt_of_val_lt","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L247-L247","doc":"Strictly dominant (smaller `val`) and positive ⟹ strictly larger. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.mk","kind":"ctor","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L244-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.toDomination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination.toDomination","kind":"def","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L244-L247","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OrderedDomination","kind":"structure","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L241-L247","doc":"Order-compatibility: a strictly dominant term is strictly larger. This is\nthe *extra* hypothesis the ordered-field reading needs, and the one that has no\ncontent on `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetDomination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetDomination","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L214-L230","doc":"**The jet filtration is a domination structure.** Concrete witness that\n`Domination` is non-vacuous, on exactly the grading the tower argument needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetVal_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetVal_congr","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L202-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ne_zero_of_jetVal_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ne_zero_of_jetVal_eq","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L194-L200","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eq_zero_of_lt_jetVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.eq_zero_of_lt_jetVal","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L187-L192","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetVal_eq_top_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetVal_eq_top_iff","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L180-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.jetVal","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L175-L178","doc":"Order of vanishing: least index with a non-zero coefficient, `⊤` for the\nzero sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.add_sum_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.add_sum_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L159-L164","doc":"**The tower does not collapse.** A dominant leading term plus strictly\ndeeper corrections is non-zero — the algebraic form of \"the obstruction\nsurvives to this level\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_add_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_add_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L151-L157","doc":"**Iterated domination — the tower form.** A leading level survives the whole\ntail, provided every tail term is strictly deeper. This is the shape the tower\narguments need: one dominant level against infinitely many corrections\n(here, any finite truncation of them). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_sum","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L140-L149","doc":"A finite collection of strictly deeper terms sums to something strictly\ndeeper. (`ha` rules out `a = 0`, for which the empty sum is a counterexample.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_sum_grade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_sum_grade","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L126-L138","doc":"A finite collection of terms strictly deeper than the **grade** `γ` sums to\nsomething strictly deeper than `γ`.\n\nStated against a grade rather than an element: that makes the empty-list case\nfree (`val 0 = ⊤ > γ`) and is the form the tower arguments need. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_add","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L121-L124","doc":"Two strictly deeper terms stay strictly deeper when added. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_add'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_add'","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L114-L119","doc":"Two terms strictly below a common bound stay strictly below it when added.\nStated against an arbitrary grade `g`, which is what the tower arguments need\n(the bound is a grade, not always the value of some element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.ne_of_val_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.ne_of_val_lt","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L109-L112","doc":"Sub-dominant corrections cannot make two elements equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.add_ne_zero_of_val_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.add_ne_zero_of_val_lt","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L96-L107","doc":"**The squeeze, algebraically: a dominant term cannot be cancelled.**\n\n`val cost < val budget ⟹ cost + budget ≠ 0`. This is what every surreal bound\nin the appendix actually needs — *\"the budget cannot absorb the cost\"* — and\nhere it is a theorem about a filtered abelian group, not an inequality in an\nordered field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_add_eq_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_add_eq_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**Strict domination (the core).** A strictly dominant term determines the\ngrade of the sum — the ultrametric strict-triangle *equality*.\n\nThis is the algebraic content of `lem:surreal-squeeze`. Note what is absent: no\norder on `A`, no field, no archimedean structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.le_val_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.le_val_add","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Ultrametric bound: a sum is at least as deep as its shallowest summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_neg","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Negation preserves depth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val_zero","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Zero is infinitely deep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.val","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Grade / filtration depth. Smaller = more dominant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.mk","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination","kind":"structure","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationSqueeze.lean#L62-L76","doc":"**Domination structure** — a filtration / valuation on an abelian group,\ncarrying exactly the data the squeeze arguments use and nothing else.\n\n`val a` is the grade / filtration depth / order of vanishing of `a`, with `⊤`\nfor `0`. The only axiom is the ultrametric bound; strict domination is\n**derived** (`val_add_eq_of_lt`), not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}